## std::iter — Iterator and FromIterator mixins.
##
## Wave 2 (#06.8) — migrated from resolve/stdlib/mod.rs Rust
## registrations into self-hosted library/std/src/iter.rx. The
## minimum-faithful version below preserves the EXACT required-method
## list that the Rust registration carried (`["next"]` for Iterator,
## `["from_iter"]` for FromIterator); the aspirational broader surface
## from the pre-migration version (map / filter / collect / fold / …)
## is intentionally left out — those methods are not enforced today,
## and adding them as `required_methods` would break every user impl
## that only provides `next` / `from_iter`. They will move in once
## default-implementation lowering for mixins is wired.
##
## Iterator and FromIterator are registered into the prelude type
## scope (not under a `std.iter` namespace), matching the behaviour of
## the pre-migration registration.

mixin Iterator
  def next
end

mixin FromIterator
  def from_iter
end
